      "description": "The first disjunct tests whether K itself is recursively enumerable. The source asks whether there is a formal system F whose theorem set equals K (the question expressed by Def6). Non-enumerability rules out such an F, but the converse need not hold: the empty set is enumerable and cannot be any theory's theorem set, since it omits logical validities. The two tests agree for deductively closed K, a condition Target does not impose."
